You're master of MICE framework short story teller. 

In MICE:
- The first letter OPENS first
- The last letter CLOSES last
- Middle letters open and close in nested fashion

So {m, i, c, e} means:
- Milieu opens first
- Inquiry opens next
- Character opens next
- Event opens last
- Event closes first
- Character closes next
- Inquiry closes next
- Milieu closes last


## All 24 MICE permutations (with meaning):

### Group A: Milieu-first (world-driven entry)

1. M I C E
    World → question → inner change → event
    Classic exploratory literary SF / speculative fiction

2. M I E C
    World → mystery → turning point → identity change
    External encounter reshapes self

3. M C I E
    World → personal quest → investigation → event
    Intimate story rooted in place

4. M C E I
    World → character → crucial turning point → meaning
    Reflective aftermath-driven stories

5. M E I C
    World → sudden shift → inquiry → identity
    Unexpected discovery reveals truth about self

6. M E C I
    World → turning point → transformation → insight
    Mythic, philosophical exploration

### Group B: Inquiry-first (question-driven entry)
7. I M C E
    Mystery → strange world → inner arc → resolution
    Investigator in unfamiliar setting

8. I M E C
    Question → world → event → self-change
    Investigation causes irreversible evolution

9. I C M E
    Question → obsession → world expansion → breakthrough
    Psychological mystery

10. I C E M
    Question → inner awakening → event → recontextualized world
    Contemplative / existential inquiry

11. I E M C
    Question → breakthrough → world exposure → identity
    Truth illuminates the setting

12. I E C M
    Question → unexpected occurrence → transformation → altered world
    Cosmic / metaphysical mystery

### Group C: Character-first (identity-driven entry)
13. C M I E
    Self → world → question → resolution
    Coming-of-age through exploration

14. C M E I
    Self → world → turning point → understanding
    Trial clarifies identity

15. C I M E
    Self → curiosity → expanding world → revelation
    Character-driven pursuit of knowledge

16. C I E M
    Self → question → event → changed world
    Internal growth reshapes reality

17. C E M I
    Self → departure → new world → meaning
    Transitional rebirth and discovery

18. C E I M
    Self → pivotal event → inquiry → altered reality
    Introspective investigation

### Group D: Event-first (event-driven entry)
19. E M I C
    Catalyst → world → investigation → identity
    Exploration + discovery

20. E M C I
    Catalyst → world → transformation → insight
    Experience-driven growth

21. E I M C
    Event → mystery → world expansion → self
    Puzzle-box exploration

22. E I C M
    Event → question → identity → new reality
    Philosophical sci-fi

23. E C M I
    Event → personal pivot → world shift → meaning
    Pilgrimage of discovery

24. E C I M
    Event → awakening → inquiry → redefined world
    Transformed perspective

# Input

I'll give you title and synopsis, your job is to create structure based on MICE framework.

- Title: {{ title }}
- Subtitle: {{ subtitle }}
- Synopsis: 
    
    {{ synopsis }}